hostapd: SET_INTERFACE -EALREADY is success

A CAP that creates and configures the BSS interfaces itself brings them up as
AP before hostapd starts.  cfg80211 then answers NL80211_CMD_SET_INTERFACE
with -EALREADY ("Match already configured"), hostapd logs 'Could not
configure driver mode' and the whole radio fails to initialise.

--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
@@ -7466,5 +7466,7 @@
 	ret = send_and_recv_cmd(drv, msg);
 	msg = NULL;
+	if (ret == -EALREADY)
+		return 0;
 	if (!ret)
 		return 0;
 fail:
